# Testing Rules - Greek ERP/CRM System

## Core Testing Standards

- **Backend**: pytest with fastapi.testclient, sqlalchemy-utils for database tests
- **Frontend**: Jest + React Testing Library + Playwright for E2E
- **Database**: pytest-postgresql with test database isolation
- **Greek Compliance**: Custom fixtures for AFM, DOY, AADE validation
- **Performance**: pytest-benchmark for backend, Lighthouse CI for frontend
- **Coverage**: Minimum 85% code coverage, 95% for Greek compliance modules

## Test Organization

- **Structure**: unit/, integration/, performance/, e2e/ directories
- **Fixtures**: Shared test data for Greek business scenarios
- **Isolation**: Each test must be independent and repeatable
- **Naming**: Descriptive test names explaining the scenario

## Unit Testing Requirements

- **API Endpoints**: Test all FastAPI endpoints with authentication
- **Models**: SQLAlchemy model validation and relationships
- **Greek Validation**: AFM checksum, DOY codes, phone numbers
- **Business Logic**: Service layer methods and calculations
- **Components**: React component behavior and props

## Integration Testing

- **API Workflows**: Complete business processes (business entity → invoice → AADE)
- **Database**: Multi-schema operations and constraints
- **Greek AADE**: Mock AADE integration with realistic responses
- **Authentication**: Multi-tenant access control scenarios
- **Performance**: API response times and database query optimization

## Greek Compliance Testing (MANDATORY)

- **AFM Validation**: Valid/invalid Greek tax numbers with checksum
- **DOY Verification**: Greek tax office code validation
- **AADE Integration**: Mock MyDATA submission scenarios
- **VAT Calculations**: Location-specific Greek VAT rates
- **Greek Text**: Proper handling of Greek characters and formatting

## End-to-End Testing

- **User Workflows**: Complete business entity management and invoicing flows
- **Multi-Language**: Test Greek and English interface switching
- **Greek Business**: Realistic Greek company and business entity scenarios
- **AADE Submission**: End-to-end invoice submission with QR codes
- **Mobile**: Responsive design testing on various devices

## Test Data Management

- **Fixtures**: Greek reference data (DOY codes, VAT rates)
- **Realistic Data**: Greek names, addresses, business scenarios
- **Test Companies**: Multi-tenant test scenarios
- **Clean State**: Proper test database cleanup between tests

## Performance Testing

- **API Load**: Concurrent request handling under Greek business load
- **Database**: Query performance with Greek character sets
- **AADE Simulation**: Bulk submission performance testing
- **Frontend**: Greek text rendering and component performance

## Security Testing

- **Authentication**: JWT token validation and refresh
- **Authorization**: Role-based access control scenarios
- **Company Isolation**: Multi-tenant data boundary testing
- **Greek Data**: Secure handling of AFM and business information

## CI/CD Integration

- **Automated Execution**: All tests run on every commit
- **Environment Isolation**: Separate test databases and configurations
- **Greek Data Seeding**: Automatic test data setup
- **Coverage Reporting**: Fail builds below coverage thresholds

## What NOT to Do

- ❌ Never skip Greek compliance validation in tests
- ❌ Don't hardcode test data without proper fixtures
- ❌ Never run tests against production AADE endpoints
- ❌ Don't skip performance tests for critical Greek workflows
- ❌ Never commit tests with actual AFM/VAT numbers
- ❌ Don't ignore multi-tenancy in test scenarios
- ❌ Never skip rollback testing for database migrations
- ❌ Don't test without realistic Greek character sets

